-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Knight Lore
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1984
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Knight Lore (1984)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         0f2006bf897b786f48e8dd3d68924046

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every figure: Sabreman in a
              white pith helmet with fair skin, a yellow shirt and blue
              shorts; the werewolf, guards, spiked balls in grey and lilac,
              stone blocks, items and the sun and moon in their own colours.
              Each room gets a floor chosen from the room: square flagstones,
              narrow stone in either direction, or grass with fences. Walls,
              arches and the panel keep the original's one colour per room. No
              white outlines or edges. Source: Enhanced colours and floors:
              the Spec256 team, from their Spec256 conversion of the game.

  Pace        original (+1.77% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe AFC7
              with IX 23560 (the player's own update); Enhanced against the
              unchanged game, 3 R seeds a scene, updates 1-221 averaged;
              single trials -0.92 to +1.82%; player state equal at all 1,989
              updates; a room entry about 0.2 s longer, then repaid; default
              is the original game)

  Changes     1.0: Enhanced figures as Next sprites with the original masks
              and drawing order, the Spec256 conversion's colours and four
              floors chosen per room; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM
              in both sets; the game's speed restored after every hook; R kept
              as the original's; original pace; the tape's loading screen; six
              checked trainers

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 keyboard, 2 Kempston, 3 cursor or 4
              Interface II joystick, 5 directional control, then 0 to start.
              The default is the original game, picture and all: its rooms are
              drawn in one colour each, so it never had colour clash; the
              patch gives it Sinclair's whole 48K ROM so it runs on NextZXOS
              26.11. Enhanced paints the figures as Next sprites and lays a
              floor in each room. The original 48K game with its beeper sound.
              Known issues: with Enhanced on, entering a room takes about 0.2
              seconds longer than the original's own room-drawing pause (0.4
              to 0.6 seconds); the game makes most of it up over the next
              second or two. Infinite days and Stop sundial also stop the day
              count and the sun and moon window being drawn, as the archive's
              POKEs do in the original. Missing: not reached in testing:
              natural play to the end (recordings and soaks cover menus,
              rooms, the werewolf change, deaths, game over and restart),
              joysticks; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite days
   3  Stop sundial
   4  Start with 9 lives
   5  Any object in cauldron
   6  Werewolf safe at cauldron

  The archive's POKEs for this release, each checked on the game's own code.
  Werewolf safe at cauldron corrected: the archive's value jumps into the
  middle of an instruction; the corrected one skips the change cleanly.

